  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ATAF - Shaping African Tax Systems of the Future</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Core support to African Tax Administration Forum (ATAF) in implementing their strategic plan for improved domestic resource mobilization in Africa. The overall objective of the program is that ATAF contributes to improved domestic resource mobilization in Africa. More specifically, the program aims are:
&#x2022;	ATAF enhances African tax systems through capacity building and technical programs.
&#x2022;	ATAF is recognized as the African Voice on taxation in domestic, regional and international debates.
&#x2022;	As a data and knowledge hub, ATAF shapes African tax systems.
&#x2022;	ATAF establishes a continental exchange on the nexus between tax administration and policy.
&#x2022;	ATAF stands on financial sustainable grounds, with appropriate structures, process, governance in place.
&#x2022;	ATAF is prepared to mature into a regionalised organisation with established training centers and regional operations.
The intended target group is tax administrations in Africa.
In 2024, ATAF delivered country specific technical assistance to 24-member countries, including Malawi, Mozambique and Tanzania.</narrative>
  </description>
